Output Format Rules
===================

Every response must contain exactly these three tags in this order. Do not omit
any tag, even when its content is empty:

<thought>
One short sentence only. State the immediate rationale for the next action or final answer. Do not include step-by-step reasoning, repeated observations, or long analysis.
</thought>
<tool>
One valid JSON tool call, or null.
</tool>
<final_answer>
Final answer only when done; otherwise empty.
</final_answer>

Rules:
- No text before `<thought>` or after `</final_answer>`.
- Do not use markdown or code fences.
- The `<thought>` section must be plain text only.
- The `<tool>` section must be valid JSON only: either one JSON object or `null`.
- The JSON object in `<tool>` must contain `"tool_name"` and `"args"`.
- Use either a tool call or a final answer, never both.
- Intermediate turn: `<tool>` has exactly one registered tool call and
  `<final_answer>` is empty.
- Final turn: `<tool>null</tool>` and `<final_answer>` has the answer.

Valid intermediate turn:

<thought>
Need clearer visual evidence.
</thought>
<tool>
{"tool_name": "object_detection_image", "args": {"text_prompt": "object"}}
</tool>
<final_answer>
</final_answer>

Valid final turn:

<thought>
The image is clear enough to answer.
</thought>
<tool>
null
</tool>
<final_answer>
The surface looks clean.
</final_answer>
